+===== path p export claude
+Project a toolpath document into a Claude Code session
+
+Usage: path p export claude [OPTIONS] --input <INPUT>
+
+Options:
+  -i, --input <INPUT>
+          Input: cache id (e.g. `claude-abc`) or path to a toolpath JSON file
+
+  -p, --project <PROJECT>
+          Target project directory. With this flag, writes the JSONL into `~/.claude/projects/<sanitized>/<session>.jsonl` so `claude -r <id>` can resume it. Defaults to cwd when no `--output` is given
+
+  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
+          Output JSONL to this file. Mutually exclusive with --project
+
+      --force
+          Overwrite the session file if this session id already exists in the target project. Without it the export refuses rather than clobbering local history
+
+      --session-id <UUID>
+          Rename the session to this ID (a UUID). The document's own session is not touched, so one document can be exported as several sessions. Mutually exclusive with --new-session-id
+
+      --new-session-id
+          Rename the session to a fresh random UUID. Every export mints a different ID; the export prints it. Mutually exclusive with --session-id
+
+      --pretty
+          Pretty-print JSON output
+
+      --picker <PICKER>
+          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available
